OL,3,GNEWSAFirst time runner aims to beat
OL,4,Agrandad's time
OL,5,
OL,6,FA 25-year-old man is running the Great
OL,7,FNorth Run for the first time after
OL,8,Fbeing inspired by his grandad who ran
OL,9,Fthe event 27 times in a row.
OL,11,FDan Turnbull, from South Shields, is
OL,12,Ffollowing in the footsteps of his
OL,13,Fgrandfather, Mel Turnbull, 82, who
OL,14,Fcompeted in the first event in 1981.
OL,16,FThe Great Run Company, which runs the
OL,17,Fevent, said the number of competitors
OL,18,Faged 25 and under had almost doubled
OL,19,Fover the past five years, with more
OL,20,Fthan 15% of entrants now falling into
OL,21,Fthat age group.
OL,23,APub: 11-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
